.TH OROC-BUILD 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.0" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-build \- Build Oro application.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc build [options] [<project\-or\-source>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Build Oro application. Provide a project directory, HTML file, or JavaScript module. When no oro.toml is found, oroc infers a minimal configuration automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<platform>\fR
platform target to build application for (defaults to host):
.br
\(bu android
.br
\(bu android\-emulator
.br
\(bu ios
.br
\(bu ios\-simulator
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml/oro.ini file
.TP
\fB\-\-copy=<source:dest>\fR
extra copy mapping (like [build] copy; can be repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-port=<port>\fR
load "index.html" from a specific port (if host is not specified, defaults to localhost)
.TP
\fB\-\-host=<host>\fR
load "index.html" from a specific host (if port is not specified, defaults to 80)
.TP
\fB\-\-test[=path]\fR
indicate test mode, optionally importing a test file relative to resource files
.TP
\fB\-\-headless\fR
build application to run in headless mode (without frame or window)
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\fR
build for production (disables debugging info, inspector, etc.)
.TP
\fB\-D, \-\-debug\fR
enable debug mode
.TP
\fB\-E, \-\-env\fR
add environment variables
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-only\-build\fR
only run build step,
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-package\fR
package the app for distribution
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
hint for less log output
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-run\fR
run after building
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-w, \-\-watch\fR
watch for changes to rerun build step
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR
allow external command execution (gates ndk\-build/gradle/git/build scripts)
.TP
\fB\-\-sanitizers\fR
enable developer sanitizers (ASan/UBSan) for desktop core builds
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-keylog=<path>\fR
write NSS TLS key log lines to <path> (OpenSSL provider)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBORO_ALLOW_EXEC\fR
allow external exec during builds
.TP
\fBORO_ENABLE_SANITIZERS\fR
enable ASan/UBSan on desktop builds
.SH NOTES
.PP
Relative paths are resolved from the project root or from the directory containing the explicit `\-\-config` file when one is supplied. `\-\-prod` controls packaging/debug defaults; `\-\-package` controls whether a distributable artifact is produced in addition to the build output directory. Use `\-\-copy` for one\-off extra bundle mappings without modifying `oro.toml`. NO_ANDROID and NO_IOS do not control this application build command. They are independent, presence\-based exclusions for runtime source bootstrap (`bin/install.sh` / `npm run relink`).
.SH COMMON ERRORS
.PP
Android builds: run `oroc setup \-\-platform=android` and accept SDK licenses. macOS/iOS signing: set `[ios] provisioning_profile`/specifier or `[mac.productbuild] identity` in your config file. If you see "external command execution is disabled", pass `\-\-allow\-exec` or set `ORO_ALLOW_EXEC=1`.
.SH LINUX OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-package\-format=<format>\fR
package a Linux application in a specified format for distribution:
.br
\(bu deb (default)
.br
\(bu rpm
.br
\(bu zip
.br
\(bu aur (generate AUR PKGBUILD only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\fR
sign Linux packages with GPG (writes .asc next to the artifact)
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-key=<id>\fR
optional GPG key ID or fingerprint to use with '\-\-sign' (letters/digits/@._\- only)
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.PP
Windows 10/11 SDK and Visual Studio Build Tools are recommended. Ensure `signtool.exe` is available (set SIGNTOOL or add SDK bin to PATH).
.SH MACOS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-codesign\fR
code sign application with 'codesign'
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-notarize\fR
notarize application with 'notarytool'
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-package\-format=<format>\fR
package a macOS application in a specified format for distribution:
.br
\(bu zip (default)
.br
\(bu pkg
.SH IOS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-codesign\fR
code sign application during xcoddbuild (requires '[ios] provisioning_profile' in your config file)
.SH WINDOWS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-package\-format=<format>\fR
package a Windows application in a specified format for distribution:
.br
\(bu appx (default)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc build .\fR
build the current project for the host platform
.TP
\fBoroc build \-r \-\-debug .\fR
rebuild and immediately run a debug build
.TP
\fBoroc build \-\-platform=ios \-\-prod \-\-package .\fR
produce a signed/package\-ready iOS build using your config
.TP
\fBoroc build \-\-copy assets:assets .\fR
include an extra assets directory in the bundle for this build only
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
